WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.650
- Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.060
Back when they were teenagers,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.780
these guys were band members
in real life and on TV,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.290
they went their separate ways
after the show ended in 2014,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.750
but reunited just a few years ago

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.940
and have become a huge success once again

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.280
with over 2 billion global
streams of their music.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.779
(audience cheers)

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:20.612
You can check out (audience cheering)

00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:22.380
I said billion, that's a lot!

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.570
You can check out the new deluxe version

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.910
of their Another Life album, it's out now,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.487
please welcome the guys
from Big Time Rush!

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:31.446
(audience cheers loudly)
Carlos Penavega,

00:00:31.446 --> 00:00:34.603
Kendall Schmidt, James
Maslow, Logan Henderson.

00:00:34.603 --> 00:00:37.473
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:40.473
(audience cheering)

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:57.813
What's up y'all?

00:00:57.813 --> 00:00:59.763
- Look at that.
- I am very into this.

00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:00.596
- Yes.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:00.596 --> 00:01:01.470
- I'm a horse guy, so.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.440
- Yeah, I'm, I love green
too, it's my favorite color.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.937
- You can have it.
- Yep, thank you.

00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:06.770
- Oh, wow.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.160
- It's actually very soft, too.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.930
But why reunite now?

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.970
Congratulations, by the way,
on the second round of success.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.860
- Thank you.
(audience cheers)

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.650
- Why did you think now was
like, the time to do it?

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.020
- Well, it's been about
three years now actually.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.670
It's something we had spoken about a bunch

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.650
and over the years, you know, the timing

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.720
with our personal schedules,
finding the right team

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.150
never quite added up, and then we finally

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.820
put everything in line,
it worked out for us,

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.530
and man, we are just so happy to be back.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.380
- Worked out, you're selling
out Madison Square Garden,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.640
the Forum, the (audience cheers)

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.820
Like, you're killing it, that's amaze--

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.940
Do you find that, what about the fan base?

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.440
'Cause it's gotta be a
little different, right,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.610
from when you first started as well.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.410
Like do you find that
they're new fans, old fans,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.760
or just a really good mixture?

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.070
- Yeah, I mean, we got
lucky, 'cause our fans

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.230
were amazing back then,
they're all older now,

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.760
some of them even have kids now...

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.947
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh, so they're
bringing their kids, right?

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.900
- Right, but then, the
amazing world of streaming,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.580
our show got picked up again,

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.660
so we have this
- And it comes, yeah!

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.940
- new generation of
kids, so now we go out,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.190
and we're in the audience, and
they're six, they're eight,

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.810
they're 25, they're 30, and we're like.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.920
- [Kendall] My grandma's also there.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.270
- A grandma's there.
- Yeah.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.500
- Grandma Boots.
- Grandma Boots!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.060
- But Carlos's kids are
also watching it, so.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.577
- Yeah, yeah, it's, got
the whole, it's fun.

00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:15.570
- Oh my, oh that's kinda cool.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.860
That your kids are, like, into it.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.250
- Oh, my kids, I mean, I
think our first tour back

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.757
was when they really were like,

00:02:21.757 --> 00:02:23.460
"My dad's cool."
(audience laughs)

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:24.720
- Oh, that's a win, man.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.985
- [Carlos] And hold on, we
did one show, and Ocean,

00:02:26.985 --> 00:02:27.818
- [Audience] Aww.

00:02:27.818 --> 00:02:28.651
- Oh there they are, yeah.

00:02:28.651 --> 00:02:31.350
Ocean, my oldest, it's
actually his birthday today.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.670
- [Kelly] Aww.
- [James] Happy birthday!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.227
- He runs up to me, and he goes,

00:02:35.227 --> 00:02:36.918
"I'm so proud of you, Daddy."

00:02:36.918 --> 00:02:37.751
- [Audience] Aww.

00:02:37.751 --> 00:02:40.800
And I was just like, "Oh my
God, I love you, just stop."

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.330
- I would break down.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.940
And it's so cool when
you're cool to your kids.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.290
Like, it's like you could win
awards, you could do stuff,

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.510
but when your kid looks at
you like you're like, Thor,

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.343
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:49.343 --> 00:02:51.720
- You're like, "Oh my
God," like, it's magical.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.940
So what about, I have to
ask 'cause a lot of artists

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.610
have like pre-show
things, y'all do a quack?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.320
What, now what do ya do?
- Yeah, we do.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.300
It's like a Mighty Ducks kind of quack.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.040
- I love the Mighty Ducks!

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.620
- Yeah, there's four grown
men making a quack sound,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.875
it just kinda gets you outta your head.

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:06.708
- [Kelly] I wanna quack!

00:03:06.708 --> 00:03:07.710
How do you--
- We incorporate everyone.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.940
So we incorporate our crew

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.320
and anybody who's around we bring in.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.797
So come on in.
- Okay, I'm coming in.

00:03:11.797 --> 00:03:12.630
- Hands in, right before we go.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.463
- Oh, hands in!
- Hands in.

00:03:13.463 --> 00:03:14.555
- Words of wisdom.
- Yes!

00:03:14.555 --> 00:03:15.388
- We ask for words of wisdom.

00:03:15.388 --> 00:03:16.710
- I have dry hands, I'm so sorry.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.543
Okay.
- It's all good.

00:03:17.543 --> 00:03:18.376
- Are those the words of wisdom?

00:03:18.376 --> 00:03:19.209
- Yep.
- You gotta give it some--

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:20.042
- Use more lotion.

00:03:20.042 --> 00:03:21.690
- What would you tell us before a show?

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.221
Words of wisdom before.
- Don't suck.

00:03:23.221 --> 00:03:24.512
- Okay.
- Don't suck!

00:03:24.512 --> 00:03:27.083
- And... Quack! Quack!
Quack! Quack! Quack! Quack!

00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:28.909
Quack! Quack! Quack! Quack! Yay!

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:30.134
(audience cheers)

00:03:30.134 --> 00:03:32.142
- Okay! Alright, alright.

00:03:32.142 --> 00:03:33.850
So y'all been doing that
since the beginning?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:34.860
- Since the beginning.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.440
Every single show, it's
good luck, we have to do it.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.966
- Yeah, since I was nineteen.

00:03:38.966 --> 00:03:39.799
- Miss it twice.
- We said those

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:41.482
words of wisdom before, don't suck.

00:03:41.482 --> 00:03:42.315
- Don't suck.
- Don't suck.

00:03:42.315 --> 00:03:43.215
- You lotion your hands

00:03:43.215 --> 00:03:44.048
and don't suck.
- Well, here's my thing,

00:03:44.048 --> 00:03:47.130
I kept it family friendly,
that's not what I say (laughs).

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.390
I usually am messing with my band,

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.897
I'll pick like one person, I'm like,

00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:51.840
"Don't you (beep) this up."

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.910
And I'm totally messing with
everyone, but it's the, yeah,

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:54.743
it breaks the ice.
- Yes.

00:03:54.743 --> 00:03:56.100
- You know, when you get out there.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.780
So wait, what's the song
that you're performing later?

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.613
Let's talk about that one.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.030
- Ooh! One of our favorites.
- Weekends.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:00.863
- [Kelly] Okay,

00:04:00.863 --> 00:04:01.696
is it Weekends?
- It's called Weekends, yeah.

00:04:01.696 --> 00:04:02.970
- Well those are fun.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:03.803
- [Logan] They are, they are.

00:04:03.803 --> 00:04:05.640
- What a great title, yeah.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.900
What's it about?

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.860
- Well, first off, it's a song that's

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.996
- Actually not as fun.

00:04:08.996 --> 00:04:10.380
(Carlos laughs and talks indistinctly)

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.280
- It's very dark.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.920
- It's kind of about getting ghosted.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.720
But you know what I love
about the song though,

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.060
is that the way it came
about, the four of us,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.320
you know, we live in
different parts of the world,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.120
so when we get together, it's flying in

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.220
and we try and pick fun locations.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.110
So we had to finish the
album, we went to Big Bear,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.760
rented a cabin.
- Selfishly.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.870
- Yeah, well if you gotta fly anywhere,

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.703
- [Kelly] Big Bear's awesome!

00:04:28.703 --> 00:04:29.536
- you might as well fly somewhere fun.

00:04:29.536 --> 00:04:31.140
- But anyways, this is
one of a couple of songs

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.270
that came out of that trip

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.130
and it really is so much better for us

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.010
when we get to be in the same
room to write music together

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.600
versus somebody writes a song,
and then you have to cut it

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.770
and kinda make it work.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.603
And this was one of those,

00:04:41.603 --> 00:04:43.110
I think it's special 'cause
we all did it together.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.730
- You know how it is when
a song surprises you,

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.610
you finish it and then when
it gets really done-done,

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.470
and then you're like, "I
think I like this the most!"

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.688
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's like a dark horse.

00:04:50.688 --> 00:04:51.840
- Yeah!
- You were like, "I was almost

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.130
gonna not put that on the album!"

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:53.963
- [Logan] Yeah, almost.
- Yeah!

00:04:53.963 --> 00:04:55.800
- And this version is
our acoustic version,

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.720
which just came out on the deluxe album,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.070
and I think I like it even
better than the original.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.300
- I always like acoustic better.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.559
- [Kendall] Yeah, it's a
completely different experience.

00:05:01.559 --> 00:05:02.517
(audience cheers)

00:05:02.517 --> 00:05:03.900
- 'Cause when you can break down the song,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.010
and hear it like that,

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.660
that means it's a really excellent song

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.830
and it still captivates you.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.030
- Yeah.
- Yeah. Agreed.

